WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.673 --> 00:00:04.159
You're all ready to make
the sandwich of your dreams.

00:00:04.159 --> 00:00:07.648
Turkey, tomato, and Swiss
on a bed of romaine lettuce

00:00:07.648 --> 00:00:11.239
sandwiched between two
slices of sourdough.

00:00:11.239 --> 00:00:13.606
Classic, but oh no!

00:00:13.606 --> 00:00:17.881
What's this? Mold? Ugh.

00:00:17.896 --> 00:00:21.125
But look, good news, the mold's
only on part of the bread

00:00:21.125 --> 00:00:25.208
so I could just cut that
away and be fine, right?

00:00:32.403 --> 00:00:36.399
There's no such thing as a
clean part of moldy bread.

00:00:36.399 --> 00:00:40.267
That's because mold is
a fungus like mushrooms.

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:43.141
The caps on the surface
are easy enough to spot,

00:00:43.141 --> 00:00:46.536
but there's a vast network
of subterranean roots

00:00:46.536 --> 00:00:49.308
called hyphae that you can't see.

00:00:49.308 --> 00:00:52.275
So let's take another look
at that bread of yours.

00:00:52.275 --> 00:00:54.833
Ugh, disgusting.

00:00:54.833 --> 00:00:56.717
Well, maybe you can
just grab another piece

00:00:56.717 --> 00:00:58.549
from the same loaf.

00:00:58.549 --> 00:01:02.004
Well, that's not such a good idea, either.

00:01:02.004 --> 00:01:06.039
because by the time the
mold sprouts its fuzzy head,

00:01:06.039 --> 00:01:08.792
what you're really seeing
is the reproductive part

00:01:08.792 --> 00:01:11.318
of the mold called sporangiums.

00:01:11.318 --> 00:01:15.351
Each sporangium releases
tens of thousands of spores,

00:01:15.351 --> 00:01:19.298
so even though you can't
see it, that entire loaf

00:01:19.298 --> 00:01:22.823
could be teeming with fungus.

00:01:22.831 --> 00:01:26.690
But it seems like such a
waste to just throw it out.

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:31.080
After all, you eat mold
on purpose all the time

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:34.462
like the mold that goes into
making cheese, soy sauce,

00:01:34.462 --> 00:01:38.374
and even life-saving
antibiotics like penicillin.

00:01:38.374 --> 00:01:42.563
Eating a little bit on your
bread can't be that bad, right?

00:01:42.563 --> 00:01:45.113
Well, ultimately, it's a gamble.

00:01:45.113 --> 00:01:47.191
Just like eating a wild mushroom

00:01:47.191 --> 00:01:49.907
many are fine, but some can be deadly.

00:01:49.907 --> 00:01:51.913
Mold is the same way.

00:01:51.913 --> 00:01:54.969
There are thousands of
different species of mold

00:01:54.969 --> 00:01:57.804
many of which are harmless to humans.

00:01:57.804 --> 00:02:00.640
But since so many types
can sprout up on food,

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:02.995
it's nearly impossible to know if what

00:02:02.995 --> 00:02:04.971
you're eating is safe.

00:02:04.971 --> 00:02:08.662
Cladosporium, for example, can
sometimes trigger allergies

00:02:08.662 --> 00:02:10.928
but is generally harmless,

00:02:10.928 --> 00:02:13.964
whereas other molds like
Penicillium crustosum

00:02:13.964 --> 00:02:18.306
produce harmful poisons called Mycotoxins.

00:02:18.322 --> 00:02:22.500
An elderly couple in 2005,
for example, was admitted

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.903
to the hospital after eating a can of soup

00:02:24.903 --> 00:02:27.548
contaminated with this kind of mold.

00:02:27.548 --> 00:02:31.671
They had severe muscle tremors
but eventually recovered.

00:02:31.671 --> 00:02:35.191
But other molds, like
Rhizopus stolonifer, can have

00:02:35.191 --> 00:02:38.427
permanent effects, and you
might recognize this mold

00:02:38.427 --> 00:02:40.969
since it commonly grows on bread.

00:02:40.969 --> 00:02:44.632
Blue green with black
splotches and super fuzzy.

00:02:44.632 --> 00:02:47.237
In rare cases, it can
prompt a deadly infection

00:02:47.237 --> 00:02:50.944
called Zygomycosis, which
causes your blood to clot

00:02:50.944 --> 00:02:54.848
and can ultimately starve
your cells of oxygen

00:02:54.848 --> 00:02:56.946
to the point that they die.

00:02:56.946 --> 00:02:59.176
And it's not like bacteria,
where a little heat

00:02:59.176 --> 00:03:02.792
will eliminate the threat,
because high temperatures won't

00:03:02.792 --> 00:03:05.160
break down the Mycotoxins.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:08.740
And since you have no clue
which one you're about

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:11.433
to put in your mouth, ask yourself

00:03:11.433 --> 00:03:13.766
is it really worth the risk?

